   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Gravity Pile\n\nSeeded circles, squares and triangles rain down, bounce off the floor and each other, and settle into a heap, with optional words or emoji of your own landing on top.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A beat about volume should feel physical, such as a pile of tasks, tickets or features.\n- A playful transition beat or bumper needs real bounces rather than hand-keyed ones.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The moment is a celebration that should shower the frame with color: use confetti.\n- Pieces should fly together into a logo instead of falling into a heap: use puzzle-snap.\n\nVariables:\n- count (number, 1-80): Count, default 30\n- items (string): Items, default \"\"\n- seed (number, 1-999): Seed, default 7\n- gravity (number, 0.2-3): Gravity, default 1\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- shape_color_1 (color): Shape 1, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- shape_color_2 (color): Shape 2, default \"#C9C9C9\"\n- shape_color_3 (color): Shape 3, default \"#7A7A7A\"\n- accent_color (color): Accent, default \"#E5322D\"\n- floor_color (color): Floor, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
